label("$\frac{r \sqrt{3}}{2}$",(-0.43,-0.5),S);
label("$r$",(-0.43,-0.25),NW);
label("$O$",O,N);
label("$A$",A,N);
label("$B$",B,SE);
label("$C$",C,SW);
label("$D$",D,S);
[/asy]

Since $BC = 8$ and $M$ is the midpoint of $BC$, $BM = CM = 4$.  But $AM = 4$, so $M$ is the circumcenter of triangle $ABC$.  Furthermore, $BC$ is a diameter of the circle, so $\angle BAC = 90^\circ$.

[asy]

unitsize(2 cm);

pair A, B, C, M;

A = dir(110);

B = (-1,0);

C = (1,0);

M = (0,0);

